{"meta":{"district":"bukhansan","source":"scripts/build-bukhansan.mjs, at 1/4 on the real place: the way from Bukhansan Ui Station to Baegundae, the peaks, the streams and the bare rock from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; scripts/data/bukhansan-osm.json); the ground from AWS Terrain Tiles (SRTM; scripts/data/bukhansan-dem.json), 1/4 above the station.","approx":[{"what":"the mountain's outline","why":"The real mountain has no edge here (it goes on to Goyang and Dobongsan): a 70 m band along the valley road and a box round the course and its peaks, the ground coming down to 0 over 45 m along it."},{"what":"the peaks' lift","why":"The terrain tiles (30 m) round sharp peaks off: Baegundae, Insubong, Mangyeongdae and Yeongbong are lifted to OSM's surveyed heights over about 22 m round each."},{"what":"the way's climb","why":"Each stretch runs between the real heights of its two ends, eased to an even climb where the real one is steeper than a walk allows (paths 18°, the summit steps 31°)."},{"what":"the top's rock","why":"Round the level top you can walk out onto the bare rock (summit.rock), as far as it stays walkable: at most 17 m out and 4.5 m down. The real top is a broad slab with a railing round it; its true outline is not in OSM."},{"what":"the summit steps","why":"OSM has steps for the middle of the gate-to-top stretch only; the whole stretch is drawn as steps with a handrail (really steel cables on bare rock)."},{"what":"level places","why":"The plaza at the Visitor Support Center, Harujae, the hut's yard, the gate and the top are game-size level pads on their real spots."},{"what":"Baegun Hut, the Visitor Support Center","why":"On their OSM spots, drawn game-size and plain (no photos of them yet)."},{"what":"Information Center kiosk","why":"Every district has one in the game. Put by the station where the road to the mountain starts."}],"parts":[{"box":[-881,-93,-18,317]},{"box":[-29,-20,20,29]}]},"roads":[{"k":"residential","w":6,"p":[[-6,6